{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"IMPLEMENTED AND PUSHED — Gerrit change 1294, commit 8cc3e9abe0 (rebased onto the current gerrit tip\nbefore pushing, so CI runs the target branch workflow against a current base).\n\nTHE FIX, and why the REVIEWERS OWN SUGGESTED FIX WAS REJECTED. The plan review that surfaced this bug\nproposed \"treat a non-empty `verifications` list as `block`\". I checked the spec before implementing it\nand did NOT take that route, because it would introduce a second defect:\n  code-review-verify.eval.yaml header: \"Per the T8-advisory contract it is scored on PRESENCE of\n    verifications, NOT a FAIL/BLOCK verdict ... either way the verifier must emit a graded answer set.\"\n  dataset comment: \"the gating scorer is presence-based, so the verifier must emit verifications for both.\"\nBOTH cases — V-real-defect (gold block) and V-clean-rename (gold advisory) — are REQUIRED to emit a\nnon-empty list. Mapping presence to `block` would fix the recall miss and simultaneously score the CLEAN\ncase as a block, manufacturing a FALSE ACCEPT. The arm carries no polarity, so no adapter can derive one.\nExclusion — the reviewers stated alternative — is the correct remedy.\n\nSHAPE: `POLARITY_FREE_SOLVERS = frozenset({\"code-review-verify\"})` (provider_parity.py:101), excluded in\n`solver_arm` (:172) alongside but SEPARATE FROM `AGENTIC_SOLVERS`. Kept separate deliberately: that set\nexcludes ops `gate_config` cannot reach, this one excludes a scorer with no decision to compare.\nCollapsing them would lose a reason, and a future reader deleting the \"redundant\" set would silently\nre-admit mis-scored cases. A test pins the disjointness for exactly that reason.\n\nRED PROVEN BEHAVIOURALLY, not by an import error. I kept the constant defined and removed only the\nexclusion from `solver_arm`, so the failures are real assertions rather than AttributeError:\n  test_a_polarity_free_spec_is_excluded_from_the_corpus      FAILED  assert {code-review-verify} == set()\n  test_the_polarity_free_exclusion_is_not_folded_into_the_agentic_one  FAILED  assert code-review is None\nThat is the defect stated as behaviour: the spec genuinely WAS eligible and DID resolve to an arm.\n\nRE-SCORE, OFFLINE, ZERO MODEL CALLS (AC4). Rows from the excluded spec are RETAINED in the artifact for\nprovenance — the calls were really made — and dropped only from SCORING; deleting them would discard live\nevidence. A `scoring_note` in each slot records why.\n                        n_gold      recall v1 -> v2            gating verdict\n  standard    28 -> 26   0.857 -> 0.923  /  0.929 -> 1.000     UNCHANGED (still 1 decision flip)\n  frontier    28 -> 26   0.929 -> 1.000  /  0.929 -> 1.000     UNCHANGED (agreement 0.929 -> 0.923,\n                                                                still below 0.95; still 2 flips)\nNO GATING VERDICT CHANGED, as predicted — the miss was SYMMETRIC across both arms, so the v2-vs-v1\nnoninferiority comparison was never biased, and false-accept was untouched because the affected case is a\ngold-BLOCK case, not a safe one. false_accept moves 0.214 -> 0.231 purely because the safe-item\ndenominator shrank 14 -> 13; the numerator is unchanged.\nTHE FINDING THAT MATTERS FOR THE EPIC: the mis-scored case was the ONLY recall miss on the BEDROCK arm.\nBedrocks true recall is 1.000, not the 0.929 previously recorded — the bug was understating the very\nthing S6 exists to measure.\nSlot-level `latency_s` is preserved (frontier 2103.3/2105.3, standard 2756.6/2484.8); only the nested\nrecomputed metrics block carries 0.0, which is inherent to an offline re-score that makes no calls.\n\nGOLD FLOOR HOLDS: 26 >= MIN_GOLD_ITEMS (20), pinned by a test so a future exclusion cannot silently drop\nthe corpus below the floor.\n\nGATES — all by exit code, clean tree, asserted EMPTY before the suite run so the result is evidence about\nthis commit:\n  HEAD 8cc3e9abe0 · git status --porcelain: empty\n  make lint = 0 · make typecheck = 0 · check_config_reads.py = 0 · gen_env_registry.py --check = 0\n  pytest -m \"not integration and not external\" -n 6 --dist worksteal = EXIT 0\n    9436 passed, 41 skipped, 1 xfailed in 474.84s\nAwaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1. Will not close before Verified +1."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785772801044899001,"uuid":"352c6cb1-c11c-47c9-9cfa-25a82ec70428"}